  "notes": [
    {
      "row": "notes",
      "title": "Why this is not just a cache trick",
      "text": "The sliding and full layers differ in head_dim (256 vs 512), in KV head count (16 vs 4), in whether V has its own projection, and in rope. Calling them 'the same layer with a different mask' is wrong — see the attention level.",
      "code": [
        {
          "role": "definition",
          "src": "gemma4.hf",
          "lines": [
            1133,
            1146
          ],
          "expect": {
            "symbol": "Gemma4TextAttention.__init__",
